What have you coded it in? You might find you get more feedback if you
supply your source code so that people can review it and compile it
themselves: Some folks get a little twitchy about running executables
posted to usenet by people they don't know. It's nothing personal,
it's just a sensible precaution to take  on an increasingly predatory
internet.

Also, depending on your choice of language and your programming
methods, you may find that non-windows people can compile and run it
too, thus broadening your userbase. (We have quite a lot of non-
windows people around here.)

Finally, you may well get some feedback about your code as well. If
this is your first attempt then your code might well be a little
messy, and you might be a little hesitant to show it to people, but
don't worry, I'm sure your audience will appreciate your efforts and
the fact that you are a beginner, and the only criticism you receive
will be of the constructive variety.



